Hi,

I encountered an issue when calling the `guiDeckReview` action via the AnkiConnect API. While it successfully navigated to the deck overview screen, it failed to transition to the actual review screen. Clicking the "Study Now" button on the overview screen after the API call resulted in an "unrecognized anki link: study" error in Anki. Manually navigating through the Anki GUI worked correctly.

I investigated the addon code and found a potential fix. The issue seems to be related to missing initialization (`startTimebox()`) and possibly a timing issue when transitioning states immediately after loading the overview.

I modified the `guiDeckReview` function in `__init__.py` as follows:

```python
from aqt.qt import QTimer # Add this import if not already present

# ... inside the AnkiConnect class ...

@util.api()
def guiDeckReview(self, name):
    if self.guiDeckOverview(name):
        # Call startTimebox() to initialize the study session
        self.collection().startTimebox()
        # Delay the state transition slightly to avoid timing issues
        QTimer.singleShot(100, lambda: self.window().moveToState('review'))
        return True

    return False
