•ë´¢"ŠQuick tips, if you are using WSL2 and your anki is on the windows host - the magic trick is setting port forwarding on windows: Run powershell as admin and then run `netsh interface portproxy add v4tov4 listenport=8765 listenaddress=0.0.0.0 connectport=8765 connectaddress=127.0.0.1`    Then in wsl2, you can test with `curl windows_ipv4_ip` .... took me several hours and going through all kinds of unsuccessful solution everywhere and finally find this one out. Great adds-on, I can finally create decks effectively!!!!!
